 The \emph{text reader} picks the option with the largest value the trace wrote; it does no arithmetic and could run on any agent's trace. The \emph{oracle reader} picks, among options whose true value appears in the trace, the one with the highest true value; it uses the answer key and serves only as an upper bound. Each wrong 768-token answer falls in one category, checked in this order. \emph{Not reached}: the trace never writes the best option's value. \emph{Arith.}: the trace's own values rank another option above the best. \emph{Incompl.}: the best option is written and ranked first, the list is unfinished, and the answer is another bid. \emph{Passed}: the same, but the list is finished.
 
